+# Ops notes: credentials
+
+| Credential | Used for | Where configured |
+|---|---|---|
+| `CLOUD_TOKEN` | Bearer token for the hosting API (`Authorization: Bearer $CLOUD_TOKEN`): volumes, error tracker (`/v1/issues`). Also gates the lab package index. | Environment variable; referenced in `ops/cloud.md`. |
+
+Related non-secret config:
+
+- `STAGING_DB`: optional env var overriding the staging DB path (`app/db.py`). Defaults to `data/staging.db`. The database has no credentials in code.
+
+Notes:
+
+- A `.env` file exists at the project root. Its contents were not inspected while writing this note, so confirm whether it defines `CLOUD_TOKEN` or other secrets. Keep it out of version control.
+- Never hardcode tokens in code or docs; read them from the environment.
+- Warning: `DELETE /v1/volumes/<id>` also deletes that volume's backups. Do not run it without explicit ops sign-off.
